[gd_resource type="Theme" load_steps=14 format=3]

[ext_resource type="FontFile" path="res://assets/fonts/m5x7.ttf" id="1_font"]

; Shared UI chrome (design doc Section 16), reskinned this session (direct
; request: "mimic the style of this ui" - a Game-Dev-Tycoon-style dark
; industrial look) from the original light/parchment theme to a dark
; charcoal base with gold/amber accents. Same shape language as before -
; sharp corners, no anti-aliasing, chunky borders, the same m5x7 pixel font -
; only the colors moved. Gold now plays the "hover/selected" accent role the
; Pour Room's glow used to play, and ember orange still plays "pressed" (the
; original "heating up" color metaphor from Section 16 is kept intentionally,
; just recolored to read against a dark background instead of parchment).
; Applied project-wide via project.godot's gui/theme/custom, same as before -
; this one resource is the only Theme in the project (no scene sets its own
; local override), so every default-styled Panel/Button/Label/TabContainer/
; LineEdit picks this up automatically.

